{\"criterion_id\":\"ledger_requirement_coverage\",\"description\":\"R01-R12 present\",\"status\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"readiness\",\"description\":\"mechanical term gate passed\",\"status\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"required_sources\",\"description\":\"missing: S05, S06, S07, S08, S09, S11, S12\",\"status\":\"fail\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"road_coupling\",\"description\":\"missing terms: inbound\",\"status\":\"fail\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"shelter_medical\",\"description\":\"mechanical term gate passed\",\"status\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"transport_access\",\"description\":\"missing terms: lift\",\"status\":\"fail\"}],\"currency\":\"stale\",\"current_candidate_sha256\":\"69ac7847bd638abfb4c3ca3429c162abd4af0f684562942528e3059b6f50a28f\",\"current_candidate_verification\":\"not_established_by_this_result\",\"evaluated_candidate_sha256\":\"d78284e6435f4bca1b22705a3f0c25d201e5f959eb3742b055cdfac4423ecdb4\",\"evaluator_id\":\"cedar-evacuation-evaluator-v0\",\"passed\":false,\"raw_result_handle\":\"raw-tool://RESULT-018/evaluator\",\"raw_result_preserved_exactly\":true,\"returncode_class\":\"zero\",\"schema\":\"stable-candidate-bound-check-projection-v1\",\"volatile_fields_excluded\":true},\"schema\":\"architecture-candidate-effect-v0\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"read_batch\",\"requests\":[{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S05\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S06\",\"start_line\":1}]\n}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"object_id\":\"batch:S05:1-70+S06:1-70\",\"object_version\":\"8319ee86b2aa90ba4d4b0a6ad91ba1b775563c783f4cce34ba97f5ade9b22f95\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-020\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S05\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S06\",\"start_line\":1}],\"total_source_bytes\":9229}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S05\",\"source_path\":\"cedar_sources/S05_TRANSPORT_FLEET.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"f9de260d4aff0081cb42bae7f938fc4fa8b26a8c653c5cdb8b57c81527057396\",\"source_size_bytes\":4476,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Evacuation fleet, accessible transport, and driver limits\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nEighteen county buses exist, but only eleven qualified drivers can report within two hours. Four buses are lift-equipped; each carries two occupied wheelchairs and thirty-four seated riders in that configuration.\nTwelve school buses become available at 14:30, after student release. They cannot be assumed in an earlier Zone A clearance. Ambulances are reserved for clinical need and are not general mobility vehicles.\nDrivers have a twelve-hour duty ceiling. A route plan that uses every driver for outbound movement leaves no legal return, relief, or shelter-transfer capacity.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nThe no-vehicle and accessibility demand in S03 must be matched to actual vehicle/driver pairs. S04 bridge restrictions can remove standard buses from the fastest route.\nFuel endurance and delayed resupply in S09 constrain repeated cycles; nominal seats are not the same as sustained evacuation throughput.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | vehicle | available | seats | drivers | cycle | status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| FLEET-000 | standard-bus | 1 | 44 | 1 drivers | 35m | roster-gap |\n| FLEET-001 | lift-bus | 2 | 34 | 2 drivers | 48m | qualified |\n| FLEET-002 | ambulance | 3 | 2 | 3 drivers | 61m | qualified |\n| FLEET-003 | paratransit | 4 | 8 | 4 drivers | 74m | qualified |\n| FLEET-004 | school-bus | 1 | 48 | 5 drivers | 87m | qualified |\n| FLEET-005 | standard-bus | 2 | 44 | 1 drivers | 39m | qualified |\n| FLEET-006 | lift-bus | 3 | 34 | 2 drivers | 52m | qualified |\n| FLEET-007 | ambulance | 4 | 2 | 3 drivers | 65m | qualified |\n| FLEET-008 | paratransit | 1 | 8 | 4 drivers | 78m | roster-gap |\n| FLEET-009 | school-bus | 2 | 48 | 5 drivers | 91m | qualified |\n| FLEET-010 | standard-bus | 3 | 44 | 1 drivers | 43m | qualified |\n| FLEET-011 | lift-bus | 4 | 34 | 2 drivers | 56m | qualified |\n| FLEET-012 | ambulance | 1 | 2 | 3 drivers | 69m | qualified |\n| FLEET-013 | paratransit | 2 | 8 | 4 drivers | 82m | qualified |\n| FLEET-014 | school-bus | 3 | 48 | 5 drivers | 95m | qualified |\n| FLEET-015 | standard-bus | 4 | 44 | 1 drivers | 47m | qualified |\n| FLEET-016 | lift-bus | 1 | 34 | 2 drivers | 60m | roster-gap |\n| FLEET-017 | ambulance | 2 | 2 | 3 drivers | 73m | qualified |\n| FLEET-018 | paratransit | 3 | 8 | 4 drivers | 86m | qualified |\n| FLEET-019 | school-bus | 4 | 48 | 5 drivers | 38m | qualified |\n| FLEET-020 | standard-bus | 1 | 44 | 1 drivers | 51m | qualified |\n| FLEET-021 | lift-bus | 2 | 34 | 2 drivers | 64m | qualified |\n| FLEET-022 | ambulance | 3 | 2 | 3 drivers | 77m | qualified |\n| FLEET-023 | paratransit | 4 | 8 | 4 drivers | 90m | qualified |\n| FLEET-024 | school-bus | 1 | 48 | 5 drivers | 42m | roster-gap |\n| FLEET-025 | standard-bus | 2 | 44 | 1 drivers | 55m | qualified |\n| FLEET-026 | lift-bus | 3 | 34 | 2 drivers | 68m | qualified |\n| FLEET-027 | ambulance | 4 | 2 | 3 drivers | 81m | qualified |\n| FLEET-028 | paratransit | 1 | 8 | 4 drivers | 94m | qualified |\n| FLEET-029 | school-bus | 2 | 48 | 5 drivers | 46m | qualified |\n| FLEET-030 | standard-bus | 3 | 44 | 1 drivers | 59m | qualified |\n| FLEET-031 | lift-bus | 4 | 34 | 2 drivers | 72m | qualified |\n| FLEET-032 | ambulance | 1 | 2 | 3 drivers | 85m | roster-gap |\n| FLEET-033 | paratransit | 2 | 8 | 4 drivers | 37m | qualified |\n| FLEET-034 | school-bus | 3 | 48 | 5 drivers | 50m | qualified |\n| FLEET-035 | standard-bus | 4 | 44 | 1 drivers | 63m | qualified |\n| FLEET-036 | lift-bus | 1 | 34 | 2 drivers | 76m | qualified |\n| FLEET-037 | ambulance | 2 | 2 | 3 drivers | 89m | qualified |\n| FLEET-038 | paratransit | 3 | 8 | 4 drivers | 41m | qualified |\n| FLEET-039 | school-bus | 4 | 48 | 5 drivers | 54m | qualified |\n| FLEET-040 | standard-bus | 1 | 44 | 1 drivers | 67m | roster-gap |\n| FLEET-041 | lift-bus | 2 | 34 | 2 drivers | 80m | qualified |\n| FLEET-042 | ambulance | 3 | 2 | 3 drivers | 93m | qualified |\n| FLEET-043 | paratransit | 4 | 8 | 4 drivers | 45m | qualified |\n| FLEET-044 | school-bus | 1 | 48 | 5 drivers | 58m | qualified |\n| FLEET-045 | standard-bus | 2 | 44 | 1 drivers | 71m | qualified |\n| FLEET-046 | lift-bus | 3 | 34 | 2 drivers | 84m | qualified |\n| FLEET-047 | ambulance | 4 | 2 | 3 drivers | 36m | qualified |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nReserve accessible capacity first, state cycle times, and preserve relief-driver capacity.\nDo not count unavailable school buses or unstaffed vehicles as operational capacity.\n--- exact batch segment 2 ---\n{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S06\",\"source_path\":\"cedar_sources/S06_SHELTER_CAPACITY.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"f82a8ad9d53d9bacf25c4dbcbc867304140e7bd40ae00dbae911347d6a140368\",\"source_size_bytes\":4280,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Shelter capacity, smoke filtration, and accessibility\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nThe four sites advertise 8,200 nominal spaces, but smoke-safe staffed capacity is 5,900. Civic Arena has 48 accessible cots, Expo Hall 64, Ridge School none, and West College 32.\nExpo Hall's primary route crosses the South Pass smoke corridor. Ridge School does not accept pets and lacks backup filtration. Civic Arena's generator has sixteen hours of tested fuel.\nA shelter is usable only when staffing, filtration, backup power, sanitation, and route access are current for the same operational period. Nominal floor area is not readiness.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nMedical accommodation from S07 and animal handling from S10 change effective capacity. Air-quality thresholds in S11 may require relocation after initial opening.\nShelter assignment must be coupled to route and transport plans; independently feasible totals can form an infeasible combined system.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | site | nominal | smoke-safe | accessible | power | status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| SHEL-000 | Civic-Arena | 2200 | 1600 | 48 | 12h | filter-test-due |\n| SHEL-001 | Expo-Hall | 3000 | 2100 | 64 | 13h | verified |\n| SHEL-002 | Ridge-School | 1200 | 700 | 0 | 14h | verified |\n| SHEL-003 | West-College | 1800 | 1500 | 32 | 15h | verified |\n| SHEL-004 | Civic-Arena | 2200 | 1600 | 48 | 16h | verified |\n| SHEL-005 | Expo-Hall | 3000 | 2100 | 64 | 17h | verified |\n| SHEL-006 | Ridge-School | 1200 | 700 | 0 | 18h | verified |\n| SHEL-007 | West-College | 1800 | 1500 | 32 | 19h | verified |\n| SHEL-008 | Civic-Arena | 2200 | 1600 | 48 | 20h | verified |\n| SHEL-009 | Expo-Hall | 3000 | 2100 | 64 | 12h | verified |\n| SHEL-010 | Ridge-School | 1200 | 700 | 0 | 13h | filter-test-due |\n| SHEL-011 | West-College | 1800 | 1500 | 32 | 14h | verified |\n| SHEL-012 | Civic-Arena | 2200 | 1600 | 48 | 15h | verified |\n| SHEL-013 | Expo-Hall | 3000 | 2100 | 64 | 16h | verified |\n| SHEL-014 | Ridge-School | 1200 | 700 | 0 | 17h | verified |\n| SHEL-015 | West-College | 1800 | 1500 | 32 | 18h | verified |\n| SHEL-016 | Civic-Arena | 2200 | 1600 | 48 | 19h | verified |\n| SHEL-017 | Expo-Hall | 3000 | 2100 | 64 | 20h | verified |\n| SHEL-018 | Ridge-School | 1200 | 700 | 0 | 12h | verified |\n| SHEL-019 | West-College | 1800 | 1500 | 32 | 13h | verified |\n| SHEL-020 | Civic-Arena | 2200 | 1600 | 48 | 14h | filter-test-due |\n| SHEL-021 | Expo-Hall | 3000 | 2100 | 64 | 15h | verified |\n| SHEL-022 | Ridge-School | 1200 | 700 | 0 | 16h | verified |\n| SHEL-023 | West-College | 1800 | 1500 | 32 | 17h | verified |\n| SHEL-024 | Civic-Arena | 2200 | 1600 | 48 | 18h | verified |\n| SHEL-025 | Expo-Hall | 3000 | 2100 | 64 | 19h | verified |\n| SHEL-026 | Ridge-School | 1200 | 700 | 0 | 20h | verified |\n| SHEL-027 | West-College | 1800 | 1500 | 32 | 12h | verified |\n| SHEL-028 | Civic-Arena | 2200 | 1600 | 48 | 13h | verified |\n| SHEL-029 | Expo-Hall | 3000 | 2100 | 64 | 14h | verified |\n| SHEL-030 | Ridge-School | 1200 | 700 | 0 | 15h | filter-test-due |\n| SHEL-031 | West-College | 1800 | 1500 | 32 | 16h | verified |\n| SHEL-032 | Civic-Arena | 2200 | 1600 | 48 | 17h | verified |\n| SHEL-033 | Expo-Hall | 3000 | 2100 | 64 | 18h | verified |\n| SHEL-034 | Ridge-School | 1200 | 700 | 0 | 19h | verified |\n| SHEL-035 | West-College | 1800 | 1500 | 32 | 20h | verified |\n| SHEL-036 | Civic-Arena | 2200 | 1600 | 48 | 12h | verified |\n| SHEL-037 | Expo-Hall | 3000 | 2100 | 64 | 13h | verified |\n| SHEL-038 | Ridge-School | 1200 | 700 | 0 | 14h | verified |\n| SHEL-039 | West-College | 1800 | 1500 | 32 | 15h | verified |\n| SHEL-040 | Civic-Arena | 2200 | 1600 | 48 | 16h | filter-test-due |\n| SHEL-041 | Expo-Hall | 3000 | 2100 | 64 | 17h | verified |\n| SHEL-042 | Ridge-School | 1200 | 700 | 0 | 18h | verified |\n| SHEL-043 | West-College | 1800 | 1500 | 32 | 19h | verified |\n| SHEL-044 | Civic-Arena | 2200 | 1600 | 48 | 20h | verified |\n| SHEL-045 | Expo-Hall | 3000 | 2100 | 64 | 12h | verified |\n| SHEL-046 | Ridge-School | 1200 | 700 | 0 | 13h | verified |\n| SHEL-047 | West-College | 1800 | 1500 | 32 | 14h | verified |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nUse smoke-safe and accessible capacity, not the 8,200-space headline.\nIdentify relocation triggers and a destination for every vulnerable cohort.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n","has_new_line":true,"truncated":false,"stop_type":"eos","stopping_word":"","tokens_cached":19351,"timings":{"cache_n":15055,"prompt_n":4250,"prompt_ms":6012.883,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.414796,"prompt_per_second":706.8156822609054,"predicted_n":47,"predicted_ms":1700.539,"predicted_per_token_ms":36.96823913043478,"predicted_per_second":27.050247009918618}},"timings":{"cache_n":15055,"prompt_n":4250,"prompt_ms":6012.883,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.414796,"prompt_per_second":706.8156822609054,"predicted_n":4